## Signal Categories

Signals shall be classified into one or more categories:

- UI
- Navigation
- Lifecycle
- Network
- Database
- Performance
- Exception
- Crash
- Accessibility
- Custom

Category assignment MUST be deterministic.

---

## Platform Source Mapping

provider identifies the concrete acquisition mechanism. source_kind identifies the semantic class of the retained event. Implementations MUST NOT encode event classes such as exception, crash, or anr as provider values.

### Android mapping

| Source | Normalized category | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `get_logs` / `read_log_stream` | `Exception`, `Crash`, `Lifecycle`, `Network`, `Performance`, `Custom` | Primary Android diagnostic source. |
| `get_network_activity` | `Network` | Network request evidence from platform logs. |
| `ActionTrace` | `Lifecycle`, `Navigation`, `UI`, `Performance` | Used for correlation and action-level context. |
| `capture_debug_snapshot.raw.ui_tree` / `capture_debug_snapshot.raw.fingerprint` / `get_ui_tree` | `UI`, `Navigation` | Used when they provide deterministic navigation or UI-state evidence. |

### iOS mapping

| Source | Normalized category | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `get_logs` / `read_log_stream` | `Exception`, `Crash`, `Lifecycle`, `Network`, `Performance`, `Custom` | Primary iOS diagnostic source via unified logging. |
| `get_network_activity` | `Network` | Network request evidence from platform logs. |
| `ActionTrace` | `Lifecycle`, `Navigation`, `UI`, `Performance` | Used for correlation and action-level context. |
| `capture_debug_snapshot.raw.ui_tree` / `capture_debug_snapshot.raw.fingerprint` / `get_ui_tree` | `UI`, `Navigation` | Used when they provide deterministic navigation or UI-state evidence. |

### Future work sources

The following are not in scope for signal normalization in this spec:

- app-private custom telemetry that is not surfaced through the existing tools
- distributed tracing systems
- debugger memory reads
- arbitrary third-party observability providers

