## Schema Synchronization

The implementation is not complete unless all public and runtime contracts are updated in lockstep with this specification.

The following artifacts MUST expose identical field names, enum values, required fields, optionality, and nullability:

- capture_debug_snapshot input schema
- capture_debug_snapshot output schema
- MCP tool registration schema
- exported TypeScript request and response types
- runtime validation schemas
- provider adapter output types
- serialization and deserialization tests
- backward-compatibility tests
- public documentation and examples

CI MUST fail when these contracts diverge.

The deterministic signal_id generation algorithm defined by this specification MUST be verified by shared conformance tests. Independent implementations given identical normalized inputs MUST produce identical signal_id values. Any change to the generation algorithm requires an explicit specification revision because it is part of the public contract.

---

## Acceptance Criteria

The implementation is complete when:

- `capture_debug_snapshot` exposes the normalized diagnostic payload described here.
- Android and iOS source outputs normalize into a common model.
- Unrelated platform noise is excluded by default.
- Signals are correlated with execution traces using `action_id`.
- Relevant signals are ranked deterministically.
- Diagnostic payloads are consistent across platforms.
- Failure conditions return deterministic error codes and payloads.
- The specification, tool schema, runtime validator, provider adapter types, and exported TypeScript types expose identical field names, enum values, required fields, optionality, and nullability.

